From: Wren <wren@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: no SEGMENT (seamless) loop seek with the hardware video sink

A looping <video> makes MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::play() schedule an "initial SEGMENT seek" (doSeek(..., isAsync, isSegment)),
a non-flushing seek sent through gst_element_call_async(). In basesrc that seek first has to stop webkitwebsrc's streaming task,
which is blocked pushing into the full multiqueue (the video sink consumes in real time), so it only completes once the source
has delivered the whole file. Meanwhile the main thread's state change for the page being hidden (gst_element_set_state ->
the pipeline's recursive state lock, owned by the seek's pool thread) blocks: a tab opened while a looping video plays stalled
6-10 s (TV: 6.3 s with a 400 KB clip, 10.5 s when opened earlier). When the seek finally completes it also rewinds playback
to 0, a visible jump back some seconds into the video.

With the hardware video sink (WPEB_MEDIA_SOCKET names its decoder service) there is no frame to keep on screen across the
loop, so seamless looping buys nothing: loop with the normal flushing seek at EOS. TV: tab-2 "load started" 6.3-10.5 s -> 0.11-0.15 s,
loop restarts every 19 s as the clip is long, no early rewind.
---
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -4114,6 +4114,13 @@
         return false;
     }
 
+    // With the hardware video sink (WPEB_MEDIA_SOCKET names its decoder service) there is no frame to keep on screen across
+    // the loop, and the initial SEGMENT seek is a non-flushing seek that cannot complete until the source's streaming
+    // thread has pushed the whole file into the full multiqueue; the main thread's pause/hide state change waits for the
+    // pipeline's state lock behind it (a stall of seconds, until the source reaches EOS). Loop with a flushing seek at EOS.
+    if (g_getenv("WPEB_MEDIA_SOCKET"))
+        return false;
+
     return player->isLooping() && m_isSegmentSeekAllowed;
 }
 
